# Never translate line endings, on any platform.
#
# Git's default on Windows is core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, so the same commit produces different bytes there. This project
# compares committed vectors byte-for-byte against their encoders and pins
# trees by digest; the first Windows CI run found the epoch vector comparison
# failing on bytes that were identical in the repository.
#
# A blanket rule rather than a list of extensions: a checkout should be the
# commit, and an exception is a file where that stops being true.
* -text
